iew Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know a lot about Beast but I love Demon the Descent and I got the screen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Anyway, I was surprised by the lack of any screen for the core game, Mage and Werewolf. By CofD Dark Eras screen being available but not on pdf, you mean you can get it physically ? On Amazon ? Drivethru ? other ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a Kickstarter reward, so unfortunately that was the only way to get it. It might be available on Indie Press Revolution at some point, though. They occasionally add new stuff.<br /> <br /> Edit: That being said, Mage and Promethean both have a bunch of quick references in the back of their respective books that are pretty much intended to be printed off for a similar purpose. You could probably get one of those generic ones and slide the printed pages in. It's not as snazzy, but it's got utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>"